messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 51 and 66?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 51 and 66, I'll start by breaking down the numbers to make the multiplication easier.\n\nFirst, I'll separate 66 into 60 and 6. This allows me to multiply 51 by each part individually.\n\nMultiplying 51 by 60 gives me 3,060.\n\nNext, multiplying 51 by 6 results in 306.\n\nFinally, I'll add these two results together: 3,060 plus 306 equals 3,366.\n\nSo, the product of 51 and 66 is 3,366.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of **51** and **66**, follow these easy steps:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication:**\n\n   \\[\n   51 \\times 66 = 51 \\times (60 + 6)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 51 by each part separately:**\n\n   \\[\n   51 \\times 60 = 3,\\!060\n   \\]\n   \n   \\[\n   51 \\times 6 = 306\n   \\]\n\n3. **Add the two results together:**\n\n   \\[\n   3,\\!060 + 306 = 3,\\!366\n   \\]\n\n4. **Final Answer:**\n\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{3,\\!366}\n   \\].Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
