messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 68 and 99?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 68 and 99, I can use the distributive property.\n\nFirst, I'll break down 99 into 100 minus 1.\n\nSo, 68 multiplied by 99 is the same as 68 multiplied by (100 minus 1).\n\nThis gives me 68 times 100 minus 68 times 1.\n\nCalculating each part, 68 times 100 is 6800, and 68 times 1 is 68.\n\nSubtracting these, 6800 minus 68 equals 6732.\n\nTherefore, the product of 68 and 99 is 6732.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of **68** and **99**, we can use the distributive property to simplify the calculation. Here's a step-by-step solution:.\n\n\\[.\n\\begin{align*}.\n68 \\times 99 &= 68 \\times (100 - 1) \\\\.\n&= 68 \\times 100 - 68 \\times 1 \\\\.\n&= 6800 - 68 \\\\.\n&= 6732.\n\\end{align*}.\n\\].\n\nTherefore, the product of **68** and **99** is:.\n\n\\[.Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
