messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 90 and 29?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 90 and 29, I can use the distributive property.\n\nFirst, I'll break down 29 into 20 and 9.\n\nThen, I'll multiply 90 by each part separately.\n\nFinally, I'll add the two results together to get the final answer.\n</think>\n\n**Solution:**\n\nTo find the product of **90** and **29**, follow these easy steps:\n\n1. **Break down the multiplication:**\n   \n   \\[\n   90 \\times 29 = 90 \\times (20 + 9)\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 90 by each part separately:**\n   \n   \\[\n   90 \\times 20 = 1,\\!800\n   \\]\n   \n   \\[\n   90 \\times 9 = 810\n   \\]\n\n3. **Add the two results together:**\n   \n   \\[\n   1,\\!800 + 810 = 2,\\!610\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:**\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2,\\!610}\n\\].Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
