messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 77 and 66?', "<think>\nTo find the product of 77 and 66, I'll start by breaking down each number into its tens and ones place values. \n\nFirst, I'll express 77 as 70 plus 7, and 66 as 60 plus 6. This allows me to use the distributive property to simplify the multiplication.\n\nNext, I'll multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number. This means I'll calculate 70 times 60, 70 times 6, 7 times 60, and 7 times 6.\n\nAfter performing these individual multiplications, I'll add all the results together to get the final product.\n</think>.\n\nTo find the product of **77** and **66**, follow these easy steps:.\n\n1. **Break down the numbers** using the distributive property:.\n   .\n   \\[.\n   77 \\times 66 = (70 + 7) \\times (60 + 6).\n   \\].\n\n2. **Multiply each part**:.\n\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{align*}.\n   70 \\times 60 &= 4200 \\\\.\n   70 \\times 6 &= 420 \\\\.\n   7 \\times 60 &= 420 \\\\.\n   7 \\times 6 &= 42 \\\\.\n   \\end{align*}.\n   \\].\n\n3. **Add all the products** together:.\n\n   \\[.\n   4200 + 420 + 420 + 42 = 5082.\n   \\].\n\n4. **Final Answer**:.\n\n   \\[.Therefore, my final answer is: "]]
